+# Working with Rojo day to day
+
+This repo is the source of truth for the game. Studio shows a live copy of it through
+`rojo serve`. Read the Layout table in `README.md` first: it lists every folder and where it
+appears in the place.
+
+## Setup (once)
+
+1. Install the tools with Rokit (`rokit install`), then install packages with pesde, both at the
+   root and in `test_packages/` (see README "Packages").
+2. Install the Rojo plugin in Studio. Use the same version as the `rojo` in `rokit.toml`.
+3. Make your **own** dev place: a new Baseplate in Studio, saved locally or published to your own
+   account. Don't serve into the shared/production place. Rojo replaces the contents of the
+   services it manages, and you can sync over someone else's work.
+
+## Daily loop
+
+1. `git pull`, then reinstall packages if `pesde.toml` or `pesde.lock` changed.
+2. From the repo root: `rojo serve` (uses `default.project.json`, port 34872).
+3. In your dev place, open the Rojo plugin and click **Connect**.
+4. Edit files in your editor. Saves sync into Studio right away. Playtest in Studio.
+5. Before you commit, run the checks in README "Checks" (sourcemap, luau-lsp, selene, stylua).
+
+## Where to make changes
+
+- **Code: always in `src/`**, in your editor. Never edit synced scripts in Studio. Rojo
+  overwrites them, and those edits never reach git.
+- Pick the folder from the README Layout table: server code in `src/ServerScriptService`, shared
+  modules in `src/ReplicatedStorage/Shared`, client code in
+  `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts`, UI in `src/StarterGui`, and specs in
+  `src/ServerScriptService/Tests/Specs`.
+- File suffixes decide the script type: `.server.luau` makes a Script, `.client.luau` makes a
+  LocalScript, and anything else makes a ModuleScript.
+- **Packages:** change `pesde.toml` (or `test_packages/pesde.toml` for test-only packages) and
+  reinstall. Never edit `roblox_packages/`, because it's generated and gitignored.
+- **Things built in Studio** (models, parts, UI made by hand): Rojo doesn't save Studio edits back
+  to disk. Export them to files (for example `.rbxm`/`.model.json`) under the right `src/` folder,
+  or ask before adding a new mapping.
+- Anything outside the folders Rojo manages (such as extra parts in Workspace) lives only in your
+  dev place, and teammates won't get it.
+
+## What to check while serving
+
+- **The `rojo serve` terminal.** Read its errors and warnings. A bad project file or a bad
+  `.meta.json`/`.model.json` shows up here first.
+- **The plugin stays connected.** If it disconnects or warns about a version mismatch, fix that
+  before you trust what Studio shows.
+- **The Explorer matches the Layout table.** In particular, check:
+  - `ServerScriptService.Tests` exists **once**, with `Specs` and `Packages` (`Jest`,
+    `JestGlobals`) inside it.
+  - `ReplicatedStorage.Packages` has `Vide`, `Charm`, and the other packages.
+  - There are no duplicate folders, and no stray folders like `TestPackages`.
+- **New or renamed files appear in Studio** in the right place. If one doesn't, it's probably in
+  the wrong folder or has the wrong suffix.
+- **Output window** while playtesting: a `require` error usually means something mapped to the
+  wrong place.
+
+## Don't break `default.project.json`
+
+The project file decides the whole place layout, so a small slip breaks everyone's sync, the
+sourcemap, and Jest.
+
+- **Change it rarely, and on purpose.** You only need to edit it to add a new top-level mapping.
+  New files inside existing `src/` folders need no edit. When you do change it, update the README
+  Layout table in the same commit.
+- **Merge conflicts:** don't just "accept both" or pick a side blindly. Rebuild the file so that it
+  matches the README Layout table. Watch for these merge mistakes (all of them happened once):
+  - typos in `$path` (for example `StarterPlayerScript` instead of `StarterPlayerScripts`)
+  - a mapping moved to the wrong service (test packages ended up in
+    `ReplicatedStorage.TestPackages` instead of `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages`)
+  - the `Tests` node turned back into a `$path` to `src/ServerScriptService/Tests`. That creates
+    a **second** `Tests` folder, and Jest can't find its packages. `Tests` must stay a plain
+    `Folder` node with `Specs` and `Packages` children. The `globIgnorePaths` entry keeps the
+    copy from disk out.
+  - an encoding change. Save the file as **UTF-8 without a BOM**. Rojo fails with
+    `Failed to parse JSONC` if the file starts with a BOM, and some merge tools and Windows
+    editors add one. In VS Code, the status bar should say `UTF-8`, not `UTF-8 with BOM`.
+- **Check before you push** any change to the project file:
+  1. `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts` must succeed.
+  2. Restart `rojo serve` and reconnect. Confirm the Explorer still matches the Layout table
+     (see the checklist above).
+  3. Run the rest of the README checks.
+- Keep the diff small, and mention project-file changes in your PR description so reviewers
+  look at them.
